REF:AM-WAP/03/JUNE 2024
Job Purpose
The job holder is responsible for overseeing airport and regional operations by providing leadership and management to achieve business growth, seamless customer experience, safety & security of passengers and airport users in line with national legislations and International civil aviation Standards & Recommended Practices.
Key Duties and Responsibilities will entail:
Coordinating airport operations in collaboration with airport stakeholders, ministries, departments and agencies to enhance customer experience;
Coordinating emergency and crisis response at the Airport and region;
Driving the implementation of the Airport Master Plan in consultation with airport stakeholders;
Overseeing development and implementation of Airport Security plan;
Driving the implementation of safety management system at the airport;
Responsible for the implementation of the Environment plan at the Airport;
Authorizing and controlling Airport financial expenditure;
Coordinating internal and external system and regulatory audit activities for compliance and continual improvement;
Overseeing seamless passenger and airport user’s facilitation to enhance Customer experience at the airport;
Guiding on resolution of customer complaints received in line with the authority’s service charter and the complaints handling procedure;
Collaboration with the surrounding community on matters relating to the airport operations;
Overseeing compliance of rescue & firefighting capacity at the airport and the region commensurate to the aerodromes level of protection;
Overseeing safe aircraft operations at the airport;
Overseeing compliance with contractual SLAs and service delivery standards of third-party service providers; and
Managing media relations in the region.
Person Specification
Bachelor’s degree in Aviation Management, Accounting, Economics, Finance, Business Management, Engineering, Law or any relevant field
Master’s degree in Business Administration or a relevant field from a recognized institution desirable
Certification in any ICAO regulatory training
Management course lasting not less than four (4) weeks from a recognized institution.
A minimum period of ten (10) years relevant work experience, four (4) of which must be in a management position.
Working knowledge and/or understanding of airport operations and management and operations of State Corporations; and
Proficiency in IT with practical working experience gained in a highly automated ERP environment such is SAP is essential.
Skills
and Competencies
Strategy execution, analytical, people management, coaching, problem solving & decision-making, prudence financial management, team work, good communication, interpersonal, risk management and leadership skills.
